title: Add named Codex session commands and generated aliases
---
Depends on the app-server launcher.

Provide the managed-session UX: `c2c start codex` is canonical; `c2c codex` is an exact shortcut; `c2c new codex` creates a fresh thread; and `c2c resume codex <alias>` resumes the named session, with an explicit exact-thread/session option where needed.

Acceptance criteria:
- Default alias is generated from stable Codex/app-server session identity; `--alias` is optional and never silently selected.
- `c2c start codex --yolo` visibly forwards only to Codex `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`; without it, current approval/sandbox behavior is preserved.
- Normal TUI exit shuts down the owning app-server and changes status to offline.
- Help, status, completion, instance persistence, and restart/resume semantics agree; unsupported old Codex versions fail clearly.
- CLI tests cover generated identity collision/restart behavior and no-shortcut ambiguity.

Blockers: P1.M1.E1.T002.